Z||000000||85ZainoGT||11-28-2001||06:03 PM||||OK, so, I have an 87gt, but the previous owner told me that the headlight motors were 86?  so...  My passenger side wont stop going down, it grinds, what can I do to fix it? thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpicNEW1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-28-2001||06:14 PM||||Time for a rebuild.  Rodney has some new nylon gears and bumpers.||||reg||1
Z||000002||85ZainoGT||11-28-2001||06:45 PM||||how much am I looking at spending?||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||11-28-2001||08:58 PM||||The type of rebuild kit you get depends on which year motors you have - the '86 and back have a large round knob on the top (the same size as the diameter of the motor itself) and the '87 and '88 have a smaller knob (about an inch and a half diameter on top) -- if you have the '87/'88 (which you should) you can rebuild it with the three small bushings from Rodney. If it is the '86 motor you will need the gear set to rebuild.<P>The bushings will run $5.00 + $2.00 s/h for one set but, you might as well get two sets for $8.00 + $2.00 s/h and rebuild them both. My experience has shown me that when one goes out, the other won't be far behind.....<P>It will take you about an hour to do both motors.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg">  <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A><p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||TRL46202||11-29-2001||10:23 AM||||85ZainoGT, I too have a problem with mine (drivers side) so get the rebuild kit from Rodney. Great guy!!!<BR> Ps. still have to get together sometime to check your car out.<P>Tom||||reg||1
