Z||000006||85ZainoGT||11-29-2001||10:32 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>The type of rebuild kit you get depends on which year motors you have - the '86 and back have a large round knob on the top (the same size as the diameter of the motor itself) and the '87 and '88 have a smaller knob (about an inch and a half diameter on top) -- if you have the '87/'88 (which you should) you can rebuild it with the three small bushings from Rodney. If it is the '86 motor you will need the gear set to rebuild.<P>The bushings will run $5.00 + $2.00 s/h for one set but, you might as well get two sets for $8.00 + $2.00 s/h and rebuild them both. My experience has shown me that when one goes out, the other won't be far behind.....<P>It will take you about an hour to do both motors.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>  im looking at rodney's site, he has nothing for that price for the 86's headlights, did he raise them? or what is it EXACTLY thatI need to get  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> thanks!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Rodrv6||11-29-2001||11:18 AM||||The earlier motors use different parts-a gear and some rubber cushions.  They are more expensive than the bushings on the later motors.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
